# Answer format (ALL projects, every reply)

Structure every response in this order, top to bottom. Never reorder it.

1. **Summary** - what happened, in very simple words. A few sentences, no jargon.
2. **Why** - the reasoning, findings, numbers and trade-offs behind it.
3. **What you should do** - LAST, at the very bottom. Numbered steps, one action per line, very
   simple language, concrete verbs (run, open, click, look at, answer). If there is nothing to do,
   say so plainly ("Nothing to do - this is finished") so it is never ambiguous whose turn it is.

Rationale: the user reads the bottom of the message for his next action. Putting actions first
forced him to scroll up and down. Reasoning sits above the actions so he can scroll up only if he
wants to know why. He asked for this on 2026-07-09 and asked that it apply in every project.

Never use the long-dash character. Use a hyphen or rephrase.
